---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Jasurbek Haydarov - Profile / Biography" 
  activePage="profile" 
  headerTitle="Jasurbek Haydarov - Profile / Biography"
>
  <div class="profile-layout">
    <aside class="profile-sidebar">
      <img src="/images/jasur.jpg" alt="Jasurbek Haydarov" class="profile-avatar" />
      <div class="profile-socials">
        <div>
          <a href="https://github.com/hexjasur" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>
          <span class="sep">|</span>
          <a href="https://t.me/jasurhaydarovcode" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Telegram</a>
        </div>
        <div>
          <a href="#" class="email-trigger" title="Click to view Email">Email</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </aside>

    <div class="profile-main">
      <h2>About <strong>Jasurbek Haydarov</strong></h2>
      
      <p>
        Jasurbek Haydarov is a Software Engineer and technology enthusiast focused on building high-performance web applications, developer tooling, and distributed software systems. He leverages modern web technologies and cloud infrastructure to create intuitive, resilient, and responsive digital solutions.
      </p>

      <p>
        His core technical expertise centers on the JavaScript/TypeScript ecosystem, React, Node.js, Python, and cloud-native architecture. Having worked across diverse stages of the software engineering lifecycle, he is deeply invested in clean architecture, developer productivity, and open-source collaboration.
      </p>

      <p>
        This website serves as a personal engineering archive, portfolio, and technical blog. Here, he documents practical library installations, architectural patterns, and engineering notes. All articles and tools are based on hands-on practical experience and continuous technical research.
      </p>

      <div class="tech-stack-box">
        <strong>Core Technologies:</strong> TypeScript, JavaScript, React, Next.js, Astro, Node.js, Python, Docker, Git, Linux, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, Tailwind CSS 4, Cloud Architecture
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
